    "result_text": "All done. The build succeeds and the acceptance test passes. The only remaining matches for the old names are in the test itself (which deliberately asserts `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` are gone) and the legitimate `CheckDigit` class (used for the CHK segment).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**New identity (`MemberId.java`, replacing `CustomerCode.java`)**\n- `of(owner)` builds `REGION + FY + HASH8 + CHK`:\n  - **REGION** \u2014 `Locality.of(city, postcode)`\n  - **FY** \u2014 two-digit fiscal year of the business-day-adjusted registration date (`FiscalYear.of(...) % 100`)\n  - **HASH8** \u2014 first 8 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName` (the existing region-and-hash hash, `ShaHex.upperPrefix`)\n  - **CHK** \u2014 `CheckDigit.of(REGION+FY+HASH8)`, a single Luhn digit over the digits of that base\n- `dedupe(...)` now operates on the member id (collision handling moved off the old customer code).\n\n**Wiring & consumers**\n- `Owner`: field/column `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id`; `getCustomerCode/setCustomerCode` \u2192 `getMemberId/setMemberId`.\n- `BuildOwner`: stamps `owner.setMemberId(MemberId.of(owner))`.\n- `DeduplicateCustomerCode` \u2192 `DeduplicateMemberId`; POST pipeline step `dedupeCustomerCode` \u2192 `dedupeMemberId`.\n- `AuditOwnerCreated`: log line and `OwnerCreatedEvent` now carry `memberId` (dropped the `membershipNumber` helper).\n- `OwnerSegment`: region re-derived via `Locality.of(city, postcode)` instead of parsing it out of the identity (the new format has no region delimiter).\n- `OwnerMapper`: removed `checkDigit` and `membershipNumber` mappings; `locality`/`timezone` now derive region from `Locality`; `memberId` auto-maps by name. `fiscalYear` is retained (same FY that's embedded in the member id).\n- `CheckDigit` javadoc/param generalized to the member-id base.\n\n**Schema & API**\n- `db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`: `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id` (widened VARCHAR to 32; postgres stays TEXT).\n- `openapi.yml`: removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber`; added a `memberId` read-only string with the full derivation described.\n\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`. Example emitted id: `NSW2716E6609E1` (NSW \u00b7 FY27 \u00b7 16E6609E \u00b7 CHK 1).",
